WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:06.050
[unintelligible]

2
00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:13.170
For you it's the weekend every day, Mum.

3
00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:16.410
Well yes, but I like it when we're all together.

4
00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:18.850
Well, we're really enjoying ourselves, aren't we, baby?

5
00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:21.410
I'm melting with pleasure.

6
00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:32.470
Well, you know, we can just prepare food, have a chat, we can open some wine. Man, they can only envy us.

7
00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:37.960
Yes, all my friends envy me for being with Mum every weekend.

8
00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:38.880
What friends?

9
00:00:38.930 --> 00:00:43.010
Just don't upset me more than I'm already upset, please.

10
00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:46.830
God, baby, what did I say now?

11
00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:55.880
[unintelligible]

12
00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:04.090
Hello, Nina, yes?

13
00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:04.450
How am I supposed to know how you feel, you asked for the divorce, I can't...

14
00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:07.800
Yes, I took the papers from the lawyer.

15
00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:24.320
I don't know, I can't come now, no way.

16
00:01:24.370 --> 00:01:25.350
Mum is here with me.

17
00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:28.090
I have nobody to leave her with, to look after her.

18
00:01:29.620 --> 00:01:30.940
Come on, don't pretend you don't know, man.

19
00:01:33.320 --> 00:01:37.770
Well, okay, come a bit later, when she falls asleep.

20
00:01:41.320 --> 00:01:42.310
Okay.

21
00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:43.350
Bye.

22
00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:45.680
Bye, we'll talk.

23
00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:20.400
[unintelligible]

24
00:02:21.100 --> 00:02:26.000
I really don't know how these women knit, man.

25
00:02:27.010 --> 00:02:30.410
I don't understand any of this, nothing.

26
00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:32.760
Will you help me, baby?

27
00:02:32.810 --> 00:02:37.170
Leave me alone, Roza, please, all I need is to knit with Mum on a Saturday night.

28
00:02:37.540 --> 00:02:39.170
Don't despair, son.

29
00:02:39.220 --> 00:02:42.150
Many people have nobody to go out with on Saturday night.

30
00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:43.270
You've really comforted me.

31
00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:46.250
Well, do you want me to go out with you?

32
00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:50.100
Look, believe me, it's no problem, I'll get ready in a flash.

33
00:02:50.150 --> 00:02:52.060
Where will we go? To the pensioners' club?

34
00:02:52.110 --> 00:02:53.800
We can go to a disco too.

35
00:02:53.850 --> 00:02:56.490
Or for a stroll on the promenade, relax.

36
00:02:57.580 --> 00:03:01.960
Okay, now I understand you're ashamed to go out with your mother.

37
00:03:02.010 --> 00:03:04.050
So why don't you go out somewhere alone?

38
00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:12.630
Because I can't, Roza, come back home after half an hour with Brufen, Apaurin, Bromazepam, Plumizol, horse ointment and fake Aramis.

39
00:03:12.760 --> 00:03:14.080
Well, you're really exaggerating.

40
00:03:14.130 --> 00:03:15.570
Okay, you're the one who exaggerated.

41
00:03:15.620 --> 00:03:17.290
We have fake Aramis at home.

42
00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:21.220
Baby, you need a girlfriend.

43
00:03:21.350 --> 00:03:22.870
Oh, really.

44
00:03:24.340 --> 00:03:34.870
Look, I was reading here, it says: you'll surely fall in love with me. My name is Dragoljubka, Dragobuljka, no, Dragobiljka, and they call me Sexy.

45
00:03:40.040 --> 00:03:42.390
Thanks, interesting.

46
00:03:42.500 --> 00:03:49.650
And here's this other one: as storks fly south, so I fly when you need a friend.

47
00:03:53.730 --> 00:03:56.910
This one has poetic talent, yes.

48
00:03:57.920 --> 00:04:00.990
But something is written underneath, is there a name, a surname?

49
00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:05.170
It says, look, it goes like this: accepts Mastercard, Diners, Visa, whoa.

50
00:04:05.580 --> 00:04:07.600
[unintelligible]

51
00:04:10.180 --> 00:04:13.960
I have a girl I agreed would come over now.

52
00:04:14.010 --> 00:04:15.280
You have a new sweetheart?

53
00:04:15.330 --> 00:04:17.130
It's Nina, damn it, she's supposed to come.

54
00:04:17.180 --> 00:04:18.940
Oh, I adore Nina.

55
00:04:18.990 --> 00:04:23.130
Since when? Because of you I divorced Nina.

56
00:04:23.180 --> 00:04:25.130
Well, that's the first I've heard of it.

57
00:04:25.180 --> 00:04:26.740
God, Roza, what an act.

58
00:04:26.790 --> 00:04:30.970
And how many times did you tell me she doesn't suit you, that she doesn't cook properly,

59
00:04:31.020 --> 00:04:34.910
that she's thin from spite, that she's from the provinces and you're from Belgrade,

60
00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:38.130
that she has bunions and has never been to the opera in her life?

61
00:04:38.180 --> 00:04:43.000
Well, speaking of opera, look, your white swan has arrived.

62
00:04:43.780 --> 00:04:45.040
That's ballet.

63
00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:46.250
Never mind.

64
00:04:53.110 --> 00:04:53.760
You're early.

65
00:04:54.660 --> 00:04:59.300
[unintelligible]

66
00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:02.360
Good evening, Roza.

67
00:05:02.410 --> 00:05:04.610
Good evening, Nina.

68
00:05:05.440 --> 00:05:08.760
[unintelligible]

69
00:05:09.480 --> 00:05:11.100
Am I interrupting something?

70
00:05:11.150 --> 00:05:13.010
Oh no, how could you be interrupting.

71
00:05:13.060 --> 00:05:20.160
No, not at all, it's very fun here and we're simply always delighted when a guest comes.

72
00:05:20.210 --> 00:05:22.970
Yes, it's always hilarious at our place.

73
00:05:26.330 --> 00:05:30.500
Mum, could you and I talk in private somehow?

74
00:05:30.550 --> 00:05:32.570
Sure, why not. What about?

75
00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:34.720
In private, Mum, we have to be in private.

76
00:05:35.610 --> 00:05:39.610
Well, fine, brother, talk in private. I'll knit.

77
00:05:39.660 --> 00:05:40.910
You can knit?

78
00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:42.220
I can't knit.

79
00:05:42.270 --> 00:05:43.660
I knew you couldn't.

80
00:05:55.270 --> 00:05:57.960
It means the two of us want to be alone, understand?

81
00:06:00.170 --> 00:06:05.980
So what do you think, I'll make you tea and you'll nicely drink it and enjoy it in your room, in your bed?

82
00:06:06.330 --> 00:06:09.700
You see, that, for example, baby would never have said to me.

83
00:06:09.780 --> 00:06:11.320
[unintelligible]

84
00:06:11.370 --> 00:06:14.430
I'll go make tea, and you wait for me in the room.

85
00:06:14.480 --> 00:06:15.570
You make tea?

86
00:06:15.620 --> 00:06:18.070
Come on, for God's sake, since when do you make tea?

87
00:06:18.120 --> 00:06:19.420
You never knew how.

88
00:06:24.700 --> 00:06:25.420
So, Nina?

89
00:06:25.470 --> 00:06:25.610
So?

90
00:06:25.660 --> 00:06:28.310
So, did you get into the matter?

91
00:06:28.880 --> 00:06:31.320
[unintelligible]

92
00:06:31.560 --> 00:06:34.770
So, a lawsuit, mediation, reconciliation, a settlement...

93
00:06:34.820 --> 00:06:35.790
Guardianship.

94
00:06:35.840 --> 00:06:36.510
Over Roza.

95
00:06:36.560 --> 00:06:39.310
I thought she could be half with you, half with me.

96
00:06:39.360 --> 00:06:41.870
Let her be with you in summer and with me at Christmas.

97
00:06:41.920 --> 00:06:43.170
I thought that was fair.

98
00:06:43.220 --> 00:06:44.760
Well, fair, how could it not be fair?

99
00:06:44.810 --> 00:06:46.450
If you want, let her be only with you.

100
00:06:46.500 --> 00:06:47.510
I have nothing against it.

101
00:06:48.560 --> 00:06:50.180
There she is eavesdropping again.

102
00:06:50.230 --> 00:06:51.510
Mum, don't eavesdrop!

103
00:06:51.560 --> 00:06:55.300
[unintelligible]

104
00:06:55.560 --> 00:06:58.510
Some things around here will never change.

105
00:06:59.560 --> 00:07:01.460
And has anything changed with you?

106
00:07:01.510 --> 00:07:02.160
In what sense?

107
00:07:02.210 --> 00:07:04.050
In this passionate, romantic sense.

108
00:07:04.100 --> 00:07:07.510
Do you think I'd be here with you if something had changed?

109
00:07:07.560 --> 00:07:13.560
[unintelligible]

110
00:07:14.060 --> 00:07:16.960
Well, I can't really say he was a man.

111
00:07:17.010 --> 00:07:17.990
More like...

112
00:07:18.040 --> 00:07:18.800
What, a bison?

113
00:07:18.850 --> 00:07:21.010
Is he a member of the human species?

114
00:07:21.300 --> 00:07:26.300
[unintelligible]

115
00:07:27.060 --> 00:07:28.230
He's very young.

116
00:07:28.280 --> 00:07:29.740
Well, he's of age.

117
00:07:29.790 --> 00:07:32.570
God, of course he's of age.

118
00:07:32.620 --> 00:07:34.170
So how old is he?

119
00:07:34.220 --> 00:07:34.640
Well...

120
00:07:34.690 --> 00:07:37.000
Twenty... what, six?

121
00:07:37.050 --> 00:07:37.470
Well...

122
00:07:37.520 --> 00:07:38.600
Something like that.

123
00:07:38.650 --> 00:07:39.730
Something like that?

124
00:07:39.780 --> 00:07:41.420
Twenty-four...

125
00:07:41.470 --> 00:07:42.840
Twenty-three...

126
00:07:42.890 --> 00:07:43.780
Eighteen.

127
00:07:43.830 --> 00:07:44.440
How many?

128
00:07:44.490 --> 00:07:45.380
Eighteen!

129
00:07:45.430 --> 00:07:48.300
[unintelligible]

130
00:07:53.100 --> 00:07:55.440
I mean, I won't have anything to do with kids.

131
00:07:55.490 --> 00:08:02.750
Okay, okay, who pulled my tongue to tell you what's going on in my private life, that's my business only!

132
00:08:02.800 --> 00:08:05.330
Calm down, come on, never mind, it's over and done.

133
00:08:05.380 --> 00:08:11.380
[unintelligible]

134
00:08:14.380 --> 00:08:16.040
No, we had very wise conversations.

135
00:08:16.090 --> 00:08:18.330
Yes, the wisdom of an eighteen-year-old at its peak.

136
00:08:18.380 --> 00:08:21.670
We talked about politics, about the Germans, about the Slavs.

137
00:08:21.720 --> 00:08:26.700
Do you know, man, that Slavs are much better at basketball and Germans at football,

138
00:08:26.750 --> 00:08:28.750
and that in handball it's a dead heat?

139
00:08:28.800 --> 00:08:32.830
You've really made progress in your knowledge of Germans and Slavs.

140
00:08:32.880 --> 00:08:38.410
Okay, okay, let's stop this, please, since I'm no longer with him.

141
00:08:38.460 --> 00:08:41.710
His mother, my school friend, man.

142
00:08:41.760 --> 00:08:43.330
Well, nobody's perfect.

143
00:08:43.880 --> 00:08:48.830
God, baby, what are you babbling? How can you say that, nobody's perfect?

144
00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:50.730
[unintelligible]

145
00:08:50.780 --> 00:08:56.800
Please, let's go somewhere to talk, I can't listen anymore.

146
00:08:56.850 --> 00:09:00.750
Well, if you want, we can go to dinner some day.

147
00:09:00.800 --> 00:09:02.420
And I'm supposed to eat alone?

148
00:09:02.470 --> 00:09:04.270
Well, if your mum lets you.

149
00:09:05.920 --> 00:09:09.150
I came to tell you we have no tea.

150
00:09:09.200 --> 00:09:12.520
How, Roza, I bought twelve boxes?

151
00:09:12.570 --> 00:09:14.460
But the little pot burned.

152
00:09:14.510 --> 00:09:17.920
The pot burned? Did you pour in water?

153
00:09:17.970 --> 00:09:21.460
Of course I did, only it evaporated.

154
00:09:21.510 --> 00:09:22.970
God, protect me.

155
00:09:27.960 --> 00:09:34.910
By the way, did that friend of yours finally find out that you got involved with her son?

156
00:09:34.980 --> 00:09:40.980
[unintelligible]

157
00:09:41.960 --> 00:09:42.270
Baby!

158
00:09:42.320 --> 00:09:46.440
Mum, when you start a fire, it's not a fire, it's a natural disaster.

159
00:09:46.490 --> 00:09:48.810
You melted the coffee pot, for heaven's sake, woman.

160
00:09:48.860 --> 00:09:52.910
That's because you insisted I make the tea myself.

161
00:09:52.960 --> 00:09:55.070
Oh, oh, it's stabbing my heart.

162
00:09:55.120 --> 00:09:57.450
Look, my left arm is going numb.

163
00:09:57.500 --> 00:09:59.760
Look, I can't make a fist.

164
00:09:59.810 --> 00:10:00.610
Are you okay?

165
00:10:00.660 --> 00:10:06.610
Now we'll call an ambulance again, and they'll say again that everything's fine.

166
00:10:06.660 --> 00:10:11.850
They won't come to us anymore, they've spent more time here than at the hospital.

167
00:10:11.900 --> 00:10:15.390
Come on, you lie down nicely, you'll feel better, surely.

168
00:10:15.440 --> 00:10:17.390
And I'm getting worse and worse.

169
00:10:17.940 --> 00:10:21.680
Tonight we're going to dinner, don't worry, I'll sort this out.

170
00:10:21.730 --> 00:10:23.160
I'd like to see that miracle.

171
00:10:23.210 --> 00:10:24.510
You just go, go.

172
00:10:24.560 --> 00:10:28.240
Don't worry about me, I'll stay here alone and sick.

173
00:10:28.290 --> 00:10:30.230
Just as long as no ghosts show up.

174
00:10:31.040 --> 00:10:32.090
What ghosts?

175
00:10:32.140 --> 00:10:35.710
Baby is always telling me about those horror films.

176
00:10:41.300 --> 00:10:43.200
How can you say that to your mother?

177
00:10:43.300 --> 00:10:44.200
Mom, you're lying!

178
00:10:44.250 --> 00:10:46.250
[unintelligible]

179
00:10:46.300 --> 00:10:49.200
You lie, you make things up and you eavesdrop.

180
00:10:50.860 --> 00:10:53.090
I see you'll be punished again.

181
00:10:53.140 --> 00:10:54.740
Well, goodbye, I'm leaving.

182
00:10:54.790 --> 00:10:57.450
I'll send you a text about where to meet and when.

183
00:11:00.280 --> 00:11:02.300
[unintelligible]

184
00:11:03.300 --> 00:11:06.200
Well, now as punishment you're not going out.

185
00:11:12.730 --> 00:11:15.900
Specialities of home cooking.

186
00:11:16.490 --> 00:11:19.660
We cook like at your mum's, right?

187
00:11:20.300 --> 00:11:23.300
[unintelligible]

188
00:11:24.090 --> 00:11:25.480
Eh, son?

189
00:11:25.530 --> 00:11:29.750
Has my blood pressure dropped, I wonder how many millibars?

190
00:11:34.870 --> 00:11:36.390
Are you okay, Mum?

191
00:11:36.440 --> 00:11:36.950
No.

192
00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:39.170
Do you want me to bring you some medicine?

193
00:11:39.220 --> 00:11:39.630
Yes.

194
00:11:39.680 --> 00:11:40.090
Which one?

195
00:11:40.140 --> 00:11:41.020
Any.

196
00:11:41.670 --> 00:11:45.440
Come on, sit here, you've gone pale.

197
00:11:46.800 --> 00:11:50.800
Do you want water or should I make you mint tea?

198
00:11:52.350 --> 00:11:56.950
I don't know if that tea is good on an empty stomach.

199
00:11:59.010 --> 00:12:01.810
Yes, brother, why not.

200
00:12:02.640 --> 00:12:04.620
But I have varicose veins...

201
00:12:04.670 --> 00:12:05.870
It's good for veins too.

202
00:12:05.920 --> 00:12:07.110
Well, you know what?

203
00:12:07.160 --> 00:12:11.430
Warm tea, warm weather outside, I don't know, but it's good for the lungs.

204
00:12:11.480 --> 00:12:20.670
It's good, it's good. You know, just try, when you drink tea, to put your left leg over your right, cross them, and then it's absorbed better.

205
00:12:20.720 --> 00:12:22.110
Left over right, oh.

206
00:12:22.380 --> 00:12:26.000
You're making fun of your sick mother.

207
00:12:26.640 --> 00:12:29.660
Oh, my son, it's easy for you.

208
00:12:30.680 --> 00:12:31.890
Eh, come on.

209
00:12:31.940 --> 00:12:36.390
Well, call Miša for me, please. He's a doctor.

210
00:12:38.660 --> 00:12:40.160
[unintelligible]

211
00:12:40.380 --> 00:12:45.650
Don't be like that, son. You're going out, and who will help me?

212
00:12:49.070 --> 00:12:52.020
Hello, Miša, hey, what are you up to?

213
00:12:52.100 --> 00:12:56.100
[unintelligible]

214
00:12:56.920 --> 00:13:02.660
Listen, I'm going to dinner around eight, I need someone to come and look after Roza.

215
00:13:02.710 --> 00:13:04.130
Can you come?

216
00:13:04.180 --> 00:13:05.770
Yes, call Jovanka for me.

217
00:13:05.820 --> 00:13:06.910
In five minutes.

218
00:13:06.960 --> 00:13:07.890
Okay, come on.

219
00:13:07.940 --> 00:13:08.790
There, you see.

220
00:13:08.840 --> 00:13:11.070
There, you see how wonderful he is.

221
00:13:11.120 --> 00:13:14.010
Even though he has so much work, he always comes.

222
00:13:14.140 --> 00:13:17.400
And that «always» of his is once every two months.

223
00:13:17.450 --> 00:13:19.650
Which restaurant are you going to?

224
00:13:19.700 --> 00:13:21.270
That's why I'm not telling you.

225
00:13:21.320 --> 00:13:21.750
Okay.

226
00:13:24.650 --> 00:13:33.520
Then take and write me in big letters the phone numbers of the police, the ambulance, the fire brigade and put it on the fridge.

227
00:13:35.860 --> 00:13:45.110
Actually, don't put paper on the fridge, write directly on it, because paper can always burn.

228
00:13:47.890 --> 00:13:50.120
And what do you need paper for if Miša will be here?

229
00:13:50.500 --> 00:13:52.500
[unintelligible]

230
00:13:55.420 --> 00:13:56.600
Hello, Joca!

231
00:13:56.650 --> 00:13:59.870
You sound strange, what's wrong with you?

232
00:13:59.920 --> 00:14:00.920
Pneumonia.

233
00:14:00.970 --> 00:14:02.510
Forty degrees.

234
00:14:03.480 --> 00:14:10.370
Oh, I thought Miša would come here to look after Mum. You know, because I have some obligations.

235
00:14:10.420 --> 00:14:12.190
And you'll send a babysitter?

236
00:14:12.240 --> 00:14:13.030
Aha, okay.

237
00:14:13.080 --> 00:14:14.710
Fine, okay, thanks.

238
00:14:15.980 --> 00:14:19.400
What's that I hear over there? Where are you?

239
00:14:19.450 --> 00:14:20.450
In the hospital?

240
00:14:20.500 --> 00:14:23.080
To me it sounds more like a tavern.

241
00:14:23.130 --> 00:14:24.450
Okay, thanks.

242
00:14:24.500 --> 00:14:27.290
Jovanka is lying that she's sick.

243
00:14:27.340 --> 00:14:28.870
They're in a restaurant.

244
00:14:28.920 --> 00:14:32.130
But never mind. They took pity.

245
00:14:32.180 --> 00:14:34.550
They'll send you a babysitter.

246
00:14:42.400 --> 00:14:45.940
[unintelligible]

247
00:14:47.900 --> 00:14:48.270
Mum.

248
00:14:48.320 --> 00:14:48.690
Mum.

249
00:14:48.740 --> 00:14:57.280
Mum, mummy, look, I'm going out now, I left all your things where they usually are, where you keep them.

250
00:14:57.330 --> 00:15:02.840
Your yoghurt is in the oven, your ID in the fridge, the canary in the cage.

251
00:15:02.890 --> 00:15:07.720
Please, end that silent strike, man, it's not an election.

252
00:15:07.770 --> 00:15:15.220
When the babysitter comes, I ask you to be nice to her, she's a fine lady.

253
00:15:16.470 --> 00:15:18.420
Mum, here she is.

254
00:15:21.460 --> 00:15:27.460
[unintelligible]

255
00:15:36.140 --> 00:15:38.860
[unintelligible]

256
00:15:39.320 --> 00:15:42.400
Move this, please, I can't stand junk in the hallways.

257
00:15:43.080 --> 00:15:49.080
[unintelligible]

258
00:15:53.280 --> 00:15:59.280
[unintelligible]

259
00:16:03.210 --> 00:16:06.160
So, this is that little girl.

260
00:16:10.600 --> 00:16:13.020
I'm not a little girl.

261
00:16:15.990 --> 00:16:17.890
I'm Rosa.

262
00:16:19.400 --> 00:16:20.770
Rosa!

263
00:16:20.820 --> 00:16:22.720
I'm Bosa.

264
00:16:26.450 --> 00:16:27.680
What do you mean, Bosa?

265
00:16:27.730 --> 00:16:30.240
Barefoot («bosa») in those boots.

266
00:16:34.550 --> 00:16:35.570
No problem.

267
00:16:35.620 --> 00:16:42.200
Excuse us, please, she's a little reserved because she's not used to strangers.

268
00:16:42.250 --> 00:16:45.630
Actually, we're all used to strangers.

269
00:16:45.680 --> 00:16:48.830
The stranger, the stronger the habit, right?

270
00:16:48.880 --> 00:16:52.340
I just hope I can rely on you.

271
00:16:52.880 --> 00:16:55.900
[unintelligible]

272
00:16:56.390 --> 00:17:01.290
Baby, is that axe still under my bed?

273
00:17:01.960 --> 00:17:05.340
There's no axe, don't worry.

274
00:17:05.390 --> 00:17:07.240
You didn't make me dinner!

275
00:17:07.290 --> 00:17:10.130
You said you weren't hungry, what's wrong with you?

276
00:17:10.180 --> 00:17:12.270
I'll make a little dinner.

277
00:17:12.320 --> 00:17:16.230
Rosa, the omelette I make, do you know what it's called?

278
00:17:16.280 --> 00:17:17.310
Egg blues.

279
00:17:17.360 --> 00:17:22.340
There, the lady will make the eggs, and I'm going to get ready, I'm in a hurry.

280
00:17:28.390 --> 00:17:29.580
I'm not hungry.

281
00:17:29.620 --> 00:17:31.380
What shall we do?

282
00:17:31.430 --> 00:17:33.760
Do you want me to read you the newspaper?

283
00:17:33.810 --> 00:17:35.370
Oh, you know what I'll do?

284
00:17:35.420 --> 00:17:38.030
Cut your toenails.

285
00:17:38.080 --> 00:17:43.580
In this house only I have the right to handle sharp objects.

286
00:17:45.400 --> 00:17:47.810
I have a problem.

287
00:17:47.860 --> 00:17:50.000
I don't sleep at all.

288
00:17:50.050 --> 00:17:53.900
At night, when everyone's asleep, I'm awake.

289
00:17:54.970 --> 00:17:57.550
Well, that's insomnia.

290
00:17:58.100 --> 00:18:04.100
[unintelligible]

291
00:18:04.840 --> 00:18:07.560
I have another problem.

292
00:18:08.730 --> 00:18:12.130
It happens that I become somebody...

293
00:18:14.140 --> 00:18:18.220
Great. And what does it look like when you become that?

294
00:18:21.070 --> 00:18:28.740
First it grabs me, then whoosh, whoosh, whoosh, and I may strangle someone in their sleep.

295
00:18:36.110 --> 00:18:37.580
Significant.

296
00:18:37.630 --> 00:18:41.930
The four women who were here are no longer around.

297
00:18:45.060 --> 00:18:46.030
Why?

298
00:18:46.080 --> 00:18:49.250
Because now they're fresh graves.

299
00:18:58.340 --> 00:19:00.660
Jovanka didn't tell me anything at all.

300
00:19:00.710 --> 00:19:04.980
Why would she tell you, she's not crazy, then you wouldn't have come.

301
00:19:05.030 --> 00:19:06.290
My daughter-in-law is cunning.

302
00:19:06.340 --> 00:19:12.340
[unintelligible]

303
00:19:16.340 --> 00:19:18.110
He won't come for three days.

304
00:19:18.160 --> 00:19:18.970
Three days?

305
00:19:19.020 --> 00:19:21.850
But that was not the deal at all.

306
00:19:21.900 --> 00:19:25.590
What deal, forget that deal.

307
00:19:25.640 --> 00:19:29.330
It would be best for you to take off right away.

308
00:19:29.460 --> 00:19:31.210
I'm a professional.

309
00:19:31.260 --> 00:19:35.570
Tell me, how much do they pay you for coming here?

310
00:19:37.040 --> 00:19:39.670
Here, I'll give you double, but only if you leave.

311
00:19:45.600 --> 00:19:47.500
Enough.

312
00:19:48.600 --> 00:19:52.600
[unintelligible]

313
00:19:52.690 --> 00:19:55.340
Don't worry, be happy!

314
00:19:57.200 --> 00:19:57.970
Bye!

315
00:19:58.020 --> 00:19:59.690
Bye, bye.

316
00:19:59.870 --> 00:20:03.420
And I'm so sorry I didn't try it.

317
00:20:03.980 --> 00:20:05.990
She and her omelette.

318
00:20:06.040 --> 00:20:09.070
What's it called, Egg blues.

319
00:20:09.310 --> 00:20:12.110
And it must be egg-cellent.

320
00:20:12.210 --> 00:20:14.340
I'm ready, I'm off!

321
00:20:14.390 --> 00:20:16.220
That's Bosa?

322
00:20:18.700 --> 00:20:20.450
Which Bosa?

323
00:20:23.200 --> 00:20:26.820
[unintelligible]

324
00:20:27.010 --> 00:20:28.910
I have no idea.

325
00:20:32.690 --> 00:20:34.040
What have you done, Rosa?

326
00:20:34.090 --> 00:20:34.240
Me?

327
00:20:34.290 --> 00:20:34.630
Nothing.

328
00:20:34.680 --> 00:20:39.420
You're doing all this on purpose so I won't go to see Nina.

329
00:20:39.470 --> 00:20:40.290
I know you.

330
00:20:40.340 --> 00:20:43.340
You know, Mum, that it's now or never.

331
00:20:43.390 --> 00:20:45.940
The two of us are in the process of a divorce, but...

332
00:20:45.990 --> 00:20:49.730
Somehow we've now started to open up to each other.

333
00:20:49.780 --> 00:20:52.250
Well great, man, see, you're doing wonderfully.

334
00:20:52.300 --> 00:20:54.380
So bring that divorce to an end.

335
00:20:54.430 --> 00:20:57.640
I can't play these games anymore, Mum!

336
00:20:57.690 --> 00:21:01.280
Please tell me, what exactly do you have against her?

337
00:21:01.330 --> 00:21:03.590
That she left my son.

338
00:21:03.640 --> 00:21:06.940
She left me because you drove her crazy.

339
00:21:06.990 --> 00:21:10.440
There, you see, you're never, never on my side.

340
00:21:10.630 --> 00:21:20.710
And when I just remember, I missed the last episode of my favourite series only because I had to give birth to you then.

341
00:21:20.810 --> 00:21:23.120
So why didn't you watch the rerun?

342
00:21:23.170 --> 00:21:29.720
Baby, let's sit down and have a nice calm talk about our lives.

343
00:21:29.770 --> 00:21:32.220
[unintelligible]

344
00:21:34.270 --> 00:21:39.240
Baby, you don't have a single minute for your mother!

345
00:21:44.400 --> 00:21:49.700
Do you remember when you were two years old?

346
00:21:49.840 --> 00:21:51.100
How could you not remember, of course.

347
00:21:51.280 --> 00:21:59.500
You had the flu then, and I had a ticket for a concert I'd been waiting for a long, long time, and I didn't go to the concert.

348
00:21:59.760 --> 00:22:03.300
No, I stayed home to change your compresses.

349
00:22:03.380 --> 00:22:07.800
There, when you have the flu, I'll stay home to change your compresses and won't go to the concert.

350
00:22:07.880 --> 00:22:08.460
Or can I go now?

351
00:22:14.400 --> 00:22:16.400
Watch out, or I'll tell you!

352
00:22:16.520 --> 00:22:20.140
Then I'll go for a little walk too.

353
00:22:20.590 --> 00:22:23.210
Where will you walk?

354
00:22:23.260 --> 00:22:24.950
Just a walk.

355
00:22:25.000 --> 00:22:26.810
It's dark outside.

356
00:22:26.860 --> 00:22:30.260
Look, Mum, please, stay here.

357
00:22:30.580 --> 00:22:34.200
I'll bring you a cake from the restaurant.

358
00:22:34.650 --> 00:22:37.680
And do they have panna cotta there?

359
00:22:37.790 --> 00:22:40.410
They have panna cotta, they do.

360
00:22:40.460 --> 00:22:44.540
It's their speciality there, with the boiled lamb.

361
00:22:45.230 --> 00:22:47.970
That must be far.

362
00:22:48.020 --> 00:22:52.170
It's not far, it's two corners from here, to the right.

363
00:22:54.400 --> 00:23:00.400
[unintelligible]

364
00:23:16.400 --> 00:23:19.400
Let's drink to the new baby.

365
00:23:19.450 --> 00:23:23.400
[unintelligible]

366
00:23:24.150 --> 00:23:26.270
Are we toasting the divorce too?

367
00:23:26.320 --> 00:23:29.580
I thought we'd put that off a little.

368
00:23:29.630 --> 00:23:31.380
Have you changed your mind?

369
00:23:31.430 --> 00:23:33.740
I'm looking at you somehow now.

370
00:23:33.790 --> 00:23:38.180
I really don't know why you and I broke up.

371
00:23:38.230 --> 00:23:39.030
My moustachioed one.

372
00:23:39.080 --> 00:23:42.720
So you see that you and I can be together.

373
00:23:42.770 --> 00:23:50.140
I've changed. Like a man I left Mum at home, came here, and she has matured too.

374
00:23:50.800 --> 00:23:51.980
Who matured?

375
00:23:52.030 --> 00:23:55.570
She did. She's maturing. Every day. She doesn't call me.

376
00:23:55.620 --> 00:23:56.890
We're eating in peace.

377
00:23:56.940 --> 00:24:00.490
We have cutlery, we have food, we have wine.

378
00:24:00.540 --> 00:24:03.510
Dessert will come too, panna cotta.

379
00:24:03.960 --> 00:24:06.000
[unintelligible]

380
00:24:13.000 --> 00:24:15.000
Mom, where did you come from?

381
00:24:15.160 --> 00:24:16.820
I couldn't hold out.

382
00:24:16.870 --> 00:24:18.590
I suddenly craved something sweet.

383
00:24:20.000 --> 00:24:20.870
Nina!

384
00:24:20.920 --> 00:24:23.050
Nina, please.

385
00:24:26.140 --> 00:24:28.160
Son, it's good that I came.

386
00:24:28.210 --> 00:24:30.450
Otherwise you'd be eating completely alone.

387
00:24:30.800 --> 00:24:36.800
[unintelligible]

388
00:24:50.660 --> 00:24:52.800
[unintelligible]

389
00:24:53.800 --> 00:24:54.800
Nina.

390
00:24:55.800 --> 00:24:57.800
[unintelligible]

391
00:24:58.800 --> 00:25:00.800
Am I interrupting something?

392
00:25:09.680 --> 00:25:15.680
[unintelligible]

393
00:25:25.700 --> 00:25:32.600
Listen, Rosa, when you start a fire in the kitchen it's not a fire, it's a natural disaster. You melted the coffee pot.

394
00:25:32.700 --> 00:25:37.600
That's because you insisted that I make the tea myself.
